  "Steps play in order.  {\"line\": id, \"with\": [...]} is a dialogue line; its visuals start with it and must fit inside it.  {\"do\": [...], \"seconds\": s} gives visuals the stage to themselves.  {\"pause\": \"predict\", \"seconds\": s, \"prompt\": text} is a pause for viewers to guess.  {\"hold\": s} lets the last picture sit.",
  "A visual is verb:argument, with a verb from series.json, or an object {\"visual\": \"verb:argument\", ...parameters}.  react:<who>_<reaction> takes a reaction from 'reactions' below; point_at:<who>_<target> takes a target from 'targets'.",
  "Lengths of line steps come from the audio (audio_manifest.json) plus the gaps below; make_timing.py writes the result to timing.json.  check_outline.py plays every exchange through the rules and stops on an illegal one."
